13. Terraform debugging and troubleshooting commands
Command	Purpose
terraform fmt -check	Check formatting without modifying files
terraform validate	Check configuration
terraform providers	Inspect provider requirements
terraform graph	Inspect dependencies
terraform console	Test expressions
terraform show	Inspect state or plan
terraform force-unlock	Release a stale lock when safe

Enable detailed logging:

Linux/macOS:
export TF_LOG=DEBUG
export TF_LOG_PATH=terraform.log
terraform plan


Windows PowerShell:
$env:TF_LOG="DEBUG"
$env:TF_LOG_PATH="terraform.log"
terraform plan


Disable logging:
unset TF_LOG
unset TF_LOG_PATH


PowerShell:
Remove-Item Env:TF_LOG
Remove-Item Env:TF_LOG_PATH


For more detailed debugging, Terraform supports logging levels such as TRACE, DEBUG, INFO, WARN, and ERROR.
